/*
	A quick and easy way to adjust specific animations if your survivor clips into the floor or wall.
	Use the macro, compile your model, then use HLMV to see how different values affect a given
	animation.

	Usage: $AnimAdjustment <animation> ox oy oz ax ay az
	ox moves left/right, oy moves forward/back, oz moves up/down.
	ax tilts the model forwards/backwards, ay tilts left/right, az changes the overall yaw.

	This boilerplate comes with the decompiled SMDs for 10 animations that are the most noticably
	broken when your model has wildly different proportions than the survivor it's replacing.
	
	These should all have the same offsets:
		Idle_Incap_Pistol
			- Laying on the ground, incapped with a single pistol or magnum.
		Idle_Incap_Elites
			- Laying on the ground, incapped with dual pistols.
		Idle_Incap_Pounced
			- Laying on the ground, pounced by a Hunter.	
		incap_crawl
			- Crawling when incapped. Normally unused, reimplemented in some addons and Sourcemod plugins.
			- Coach is the only survivor who doesn't have or define this animation.

	These should both have the same offsets:
		Die_Incap
			- Dying while incapped.
		Defib_jolt
			- Getting shocked by the defibrillator when dead.

	These should all have unique offsets based on the model you're replacing:
		Idle_Incap_Hanging1
			- Hanging from a ledge, forearms on the ground.
		Idle_Incap_Hanging2
			- Hanging from a ledge, two hands.
		Idle_Incap_Hanging3
			- Hanging from a ledge, one hand.
		Die_Standing
			- Falling and dying while standing.

	If I missed an animation, you can add your own by placing the decompiled SMD to the 
	anim folder of the survivor you're replacing, then replace the $declaresequence line 
	with the $sequence block from the decompiled mdl of the animation set. Use the existing
	$sequence blocks as a reference.
*/

$definemacro AnimAdjustment anim ox oy oz ax ay az \\
$continue $anim$ origin $ox$ $oy$ $oz$ \\
$continue $anim$ angles $ax$ $ay$ $az$ \\
